I want to merge this change because I have came across strange behavior for WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL fulfillments. Consider this example from recent 3.21 version (saleor git hash 4d0ab24):
```
{
  "data": {
    "order": {
      "fulfillments": [
        {
          "status": "WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL",
          "lines": [
            {
              "quantity": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "quantityFulfilled": 1,
          "quantityToFulfill": 0
        }
      ],
      "status": "PARTIALLY_FULFILLED"
    }
  }
}
```

Here we have an order with one WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL fulfillment and the status for entire order is PARTIALLY_FULFILLED which is counter intuitive. This PR updates this logic so that:
- If **all** fulfillments are WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL then order is UNFULFILLED
- If **some**  fulfillments are WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL then order is PARTIALLY_FULFILLED

EDIT: I have also added a fix to prevent from overriding UNCONFIRMED status when WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL fulfillment is created. 

# Impact

No migrations or schema changes.

Needed to update one test. It was having **empty** waiting for approval fulfillment. Under new logic it doesn't affect anything. Also I suppose that empty waiting for approval fulfillment shouldn't really exist? 

# Docs

Update for migration guide: https://github.com/saleor/saleor-docs/pull/1498

